Z||000000||Ed||04-24-2000||09:45 PM||||I had some A/C hardware and the refrigerant replaced at the end of last summer.  Worked fine.  <P>Now, with the start of the warm season I've started using my A/C again.  Twice I've had the air flow out the vents pretty much shut down after maybe 30 minutes of use.  The blower was still turning.<P>Can the heat exchanger frost up and impede air flow?  That's what appears to me to be happening.  Maybe the outside air isn't warm enough to keep it frostless.<P>Suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||04-24-2000||10:55 PM||||If they did not evacuate it properly and some mointure got into the system it will freeze in the line causing it to blow warm since the freon is no longer circulating||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||04-24-2000||11:28 PM||||Its more like the blower isn't blowing, although it is.  The pitch actually changes, and the volume of air coming out of the vents is reduced. I've tried switching the A/C and vent controls, thinking that maybe the various internal doors have shifted during use, but still no air comes out.<P>I haven't tried moving the controls to the heat or defrost position, maybe I'll try that next to see if with those doors open, the A/C core is bypassed and the blower will still blow.  <P>Still open to suggestions.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sdm1964||04-25-2000||10:00 PM||||I had a truck that did that, not sure, i think too much refrigerant makes it hot not cold||||reg||1
